---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const concepts = [
 ['Shaper', 'Shapes the feature: what changes, how it should work, and which product, UX, or technical decisions matter.'],
 ['Intent', 'Captures the shaped feature precisely enough for Kogen to build it autonomously.'],
 ['Build', 'Implements the Intent, checks the result, independently reviews it, and reworks it when necessary.'],
 ['Commit', 'The checked and accepted implementation of one Intent.'],
];
---
<Base><main id="main" class="wrap">
 <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline"><div><p class="eyebrow">Shape with your agent</p><h1 id="headline">Shape the feature.<br/>Leave the build<br class="desktop-break"/> to Kogen.</h1><p class="intro">Make the product and UX decisions that define the feature. Specify technical decisions when they matter. Kogen handles the implementation, checking, independent review, rework, and resulting commit.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/get-started/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/KogenAI/kogen">View source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><figure class="kit"><img src="/brand/kogen-kit-black.svg" alt="The Kogen model kit: separate K-shaped parts held in a sprue, ready to assemble." width="420" height="434" fetchpriority="high" /></figure></section>
 <section id="how-it-works" class="process"><div class="section-heading"><h2>One shaped feature.<br/>One accepted commit.</h2><p>You approve the Intent.<br/>Kogen takes the Build from there.</p></div><ol class="concepts">{concepts.map(([name,description],i)=><li><span class="number">0{i+1}<span aria-hidden="true">{i<3?' →':' ↳'}</span></span><h3>{name}</h3><p>{description}</p></li>)}</ol><p class="approval-note">Shape → Approve → Build → Commit. Checks and independent review happen inside the Build, before the Commit.</p></section>
 <section class="development" id="get-started"><div><p class="eyebrow">Get started</p><h2>Start with<br>your agent.</h2></div><div><p>Use an agent in the interface you prefer, such as ChatGPT. It needs command-line access to set up Kogen, help shape and refine the feature, and run the approved Build.</p><pre class="start-prompt"><code>Read https://kogen.dev/get-started/ and help me set up Kogen in this repository. Help me shape and refine my feature, show me the Intent for approval, then run the Build and wait for its result. Make the implementation through Kogen.</code></pre><a href="/get-started/">Install and build your first feature <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
 </main></Base>